{"reply":"You can acknowledge the effort without treating it as a reason to give up your voice. Try:

> “I recognize that you’ve been carrying a lot of responsibility for this project, and I appreciate the work you’ve put in. When the plan changed after our planning meetings ended, I felt unsure about how decisions were being made. I’d like to understand the reasoning and have a chance to contribute before we settle on the next step—not as a criticism of you, but because my input matters to the work too.”

This keeps the focus on the process and your need for participation, rather than judging their character. If they respond by saying they’re carrying the burden for everyone, you could add: “I hear that, and I don’t want to minimize it. At the same time, sharing the decision-making would help me support the project more effectively.”","memory":{"kind":"no_memory_candidate","reason_code":"automatic_capture_disabled"}}

